CBS News confirms the Justice Department  has opened a criminal investigation to  find out how its own probe of Russian  election interference began in 2016 the  FBI and intelligence agencies found  Russia acted to help president Trump's  campaign but the president claims he was  the investigators original target Paula  Reed is at the White House Paula what  does this mean for the president and the  new CBS News has learned that the  prosecutor overseeing this case will now  have the power to subpoena witness  testimony and documents and even in  panel a grand jury and filed criminal  charges so this is a political win for  President Trump who for two years has  railed against the legitimacy of the  Russia investigation insisting that it  was started by deep state intelligence  officials who wanted to prevent his  election but in a statement House  Judiciary Committee Chairman Jerry  Nadler and House Intelligence Committee  Chairman Adam Schiff said these reports  if true raised profound new concerns  that the Department of Justice under a G  bar has lost its independence and become  a vehicle for president Trump's  political revenge Attorney General  William bar has closely overseen this  investigation even traveled to Italy to  personally secure its assistance he also  asked President Trump to reach out to  foreign leaders including Australia to  ask for their help in this matter  Paula where could this criminal probe  lead and could there be charges it's  unclear what criminal charges Anthony  could be filed against the officials who  were involved in the early months of  this probe sources have suggested in  recent weeks that it's actually unlikely  any criminal charges will be filed but  by opening a criminal investigation and  gathering just enough damaging  information the Attorney General could  still hand President Trump a political  win right in the middle of the 20/20  campaign season  all right Paula thank you
 

